** Verify Docker Version 
  docker -v

** Create a container 
  docker run container_name

** List containers 
  docker ps
  OR
  docker container ps

** List all the currently running docker containers 
  docker ps -a 
  OR
  docker container ps -a

** List all containers that are currently available on te system 
  docker ls -a

** List all images installed on the system 
  docker image ls
  OR 
  docker images

** Delete 1 or more Containers
  1. docker ps -a 
  2. docker rm image_id OR docker container rm image_id
  3. docker ps -a


** Delete image 
  1. docker image ls 
  2. docker image rm container_id OR docker rmi image_id

** Run a container and interact with it 
  docker run -it image_id

** Launch a container and delete automatically 
  docker run -it --rm image_id

** Re-Run a container
  docker start image_id

** Stop a container
  docker stop image_id

** Acces the container and work on it (already started)
  docker exec -it image_id bash 

** Re-launch and interact with teh container in one line command
  docker start -ai image_id
  
  



